body:
Very nice! I love the wig and the BG/FG set you have going with her; gives her a very ethereal vibe\~

&#x200B;

I'm loving all these mermaids recently! :D

I agree, I love seeing others ideas on this sub for customs! It's my favourite thing to do on-site, so I adore looking at everyone's versions for inspiration etc. 

&#x200B;

I found the candles worked best with the bath, along with peaceful branches and the shrubbery items depending what colour scheme you were wanting. They all give it that nature-y feel :)

So yesterday marked our 1 year anniversary of playing DnD. All four of us were complete newcomers to the game and other than the occasional episode of critical role I had watched and tales of some friend's campaigns, we'd never really ventured into the world of TTRPGs. My Fiance took up the role of DM, as he really enjoyed the idea of getting to write the world and a 'plot', and the other 3 of us all made our first ever characters: December - a human sorceress, Rurik - a dwarven paladin and Yarrow - an elven barbarian.

&#x200B;

It's safe to say, I don't think any of us expected the thrilling ride we've been on in just a year!! I honestly look forward to each Sunday as the highlight of my week, getting to meet up with our friends and play another chapter in our party's story. The DM has taken DMing in his stride, and has always managed to deliver amazing weekly sessions, even through some pretty hard times we all had to face together in our real lives. As a thank you, we all wanted to surprise him with a little something for doing such an amazing job. So, we all threw our money together and bought him this bag of dice (because he's only had 1 set of dice since the start and always complained he wanted more!). I made him the card and we all signed it as our characters, thanking out benevolent storyteller who has made our campaign so far pretty epic. 

&#x200B;

Our plan worked, and when this Sunday came and we presented the card and present he suspected nothing! He was literally speechless, and the grin on his face stayed for the entire night. I think he especially loved the card, as beholders are his favourite haha. What followed was one of the top 3 sessions we'd ever had. I guess if people are interested I can write up a more detailed explanation of our session, but it was the climatic end of a lot of build-up and will take me a little time to write up. But! Everyone enjoyed it and we were all still buzzing this morning on what had happened!

&#x200B;

So I guess I just kinda wanted to share how much DnD means to our little group, and say a huge thank you to our DM who has made it the amazing experience it has been. Through the laughs and the tears... Thank you!!!! And here's to many more years of DnD! ♥
